IMPORT prelude

-- Transfer of Land Act 1893 (Western Australia) -- the registered owner's and the buyer's questions: when the land passes
-- and who has priority (ss 52(2), 53, 58, 146-150), what the registered title is free of and what still binds it
-- (ss 68, 134), who can take the land back and who pays when it is lost (ss 199, 201, 211, 214A), joint tenants, tenants in
-- common and "no survivorship" (ss 60, 61), how the land reaches the register after a death (ss 187, 219, 220, 227), the
-- mortgage and the mortgagor's position on default (ss 88, 105, 105AA, 106-110, 113, 121-123, 131), and caveats as they
-- affect the owner (ss 138, 138A-138D, 139, 140, 142).
--
-- SEAT: the registered proprietor -- the owner, a joint tenant or tenant in common, the mortgagor -- and the buyer who is
-- about to become one. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "Has the land passed to me?", "Am I bound by
-- this interest though it is not on my title?", "How do I get onto the register now that my joint owner has died?", "May my
-- lender sell my land?", "Will this caveat lapse?". Where the Act hands a judgment to the Commissioner, the Registrar or the
-- Supreme Court (the Commissioner's satisfaction under s 227; the Commissioner's opinion under s 142; whether there was
-- "fraud" under s 68), that judgment is asked as a fact and the answer is conditional on it.
--
-- Provisions covered: ss 52(2), 53(2), 58, 60, 61(1)-(3), 68(1), (1A), 88, 105(1)-(5), 105AA, 106(1), (2), 107, 108, 109(1),
-- 110, 113, 121(1), (1A), 122, 123, 131, 134, 138(3), (4), 138A, 138B, 138D, 139, 140, 142, 146, 148, 149, 187(1)-(3), 199,
-- 201(1)-(3), 202, 211(1), (2), 214A, 219, 220, 227.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 49493, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49493.txt. The deposit names no compilation number; its compilation table ends with
-- the Petroleum Legislation Amendment Act 2024 Pt 5 Div 13 (other than s 424(4)), in force 28 May 2026; the last reprint
-- listed is Reprint 11 as at 8 January 2016. The uncommenced provisions (Transfer of Land Amendment Act 2003 ss 43, 46, 56,
-- 57; Community Titles Act 2018 s 253; Petroleum Legislation Amendment Act 2024 s 424(4); Evidence Act 2025 s 492(2)) are
-- not shown or encoded. No regulations set a number used here; the Transfer of Land Regulations (prescribed electronic
-- service, fees) and the approved forms are not deposited, and "a way prescribed by the regulations" is asked as a fact.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: bringing land under the Act (Part II); Crown land (s 68(2)-(4), Part IIIA, Part IIIB and every Crown land
-- qualification); conditional tenure land (Land Administration Act 1997 Part 6 Div 2, which qualifies ss 106-108); leases,
-- easements, restrictive covenants, carbon rights and plantation interests beyond s 68(1A); annuity charges; the mortgagee's
-- possession, ejectment and the abolished distress (ss 111, 112, 112A); actions on the mortgage (ss 116-120); caveats
-- against bringing land under the Act and the Commissioner's s 141A notice; powers of attorney and witnessing (ss 143-145);
-- surveys and boundaries (Part VIII); the Registrar's and Commissioner's powers, fees and requirements; s 196 (cases where
-- the State is not liable); title by adverse possession (ss 222, 223); the Strata Titles Act 1985 and Community Titles Act
-- 2018 (which c081 and k076 also ask about). The right of survivorship itself -- that the surviving joint tenant takes the
-- whole -- is NOT stated anywhere in the deposited text; s 60 deems joint proprietors joint tenants and s 227 gives the
-- survivor a route onto the register, and this encoding asserts only that.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) -- title, mortgage, caveats and death`

§§ `52(2), 53, 58 -- when the land passes, and who comes first`

-- s 52(2): an instrument "is registered when a memorandum referred to in section 56 in relation to the original instrument
-- has been entered in the Register on the certificate".
-- s 58: "No instrument until registered in manner herein provided shall be effectual to pass any estate or interest in any
-- land under the operation of this Act or to render such land liable to any mortgage or charge ... but upon such
-- registration the estate or interest comprised in the instrument shall pass or as the case may be the land shall become
-- liable". (Signing the contract and paying the price at settlement pass nothing under this Act; registration does.)
@export Has the land passed to me under my transfer (Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA) ss 52(2), 58)?
GIVEN `a memorandum of my transfer is entered in the Register on the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has entered the memorandum of your transfer on the certificate of title (that is, it is registered)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the land passed to me` IF
    `a memorandum of my transfer is entered in the Register on the certificate`

-- s 53(2): instruments affecting the same estate or interest "have priority as between each other according to the time
-- of registration and not according to the date of the instrument, notwithstanding any actual or constructive notice".
-- So neither the date of the instruments nor what anyone knew is an input.
@export Does my instrument have priority over another instrument affecting the same land (s 53(2))?
GIVEN `the time my instrument was registered` IS A NUMBER @desc When your instrument was registered (any consistent clock, for example minutes since some moment)
      `the time the other instrument was registered` IS A NUMBER @desc When the other instrument was registered, on the same clock
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my instrument have priority` IF
    `the time my instrument was registered` LESS THAN `the time the other instrument was registered`

§§ `146, 148, 149 -- the buyer's search and 48-hour stay`

-- s 148: "Any person proposing to deal for value with a proprietor may with the consent in writing of such proprietor ...
-- lodge with the application for search certificate an application for stay of registration"; "if the result of the search
-- shows that the proprietor is free to deal" the Registrar signs an order "staying registration of any instrument affecting
-- the land ... for 48 hours from the time mentioned in the search certificate".
-- s 149: "If within the said period of 48 hours a properly perfected instrument effecting the proposed dealing be duly lodged
-- for registration such instrument shall have priority over any other instrument which may be lodged for registration after
-- the time mentioned in the search certificate and the same shall be registered notwithstanding any caveat, court order or
-- application by assignee in bankruptcy which may have been lodged ... after the time mentioned in such search certificate."
-- "Within 48 hours" is read as at most 48 hours after the time in the search certificate.
`the stay period in hours` MEANS 48

@export As a buyer with a 48-hour stay, does my transfer take priority over anything lodged after my search, caveats included (ss 148, 149)?
GIVEN `I am dealing for value with the proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are buying (or otherwise dealing for value) from the registered proprietor
      `the proprietor consented in writing to the stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proprietor (or their agent authorised in writing) consented in writing to your stay application
      `the search showed the proprietor free to deal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the search certificate showed the proprietor free to deal with the land
      `hours from the search certificate time to my lodging` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours between the time stated in the search certificate and the lodging of your transfer
      `my transfer was properly perfected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your transfer was complete and in order for registration when lodged
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my transfer take priority under the stay` IF
        `I am dealing for value with the proprietor`
    AND `the proprietor consented in writing to the stay`
    AND `the search showed the proprietor free to deal`
    AND `my transfer was properly perfected`
    AND `hours from the search certificate time to my lodging` AT MOST `the stay period in hours`

§§ `68, 134 -- what my registered title is free of, and what still binds it`

-- s 68(1): the registered proprietor "shall except in case of fraud hold the same subject to such encumbrances as may be
-- notified on the registered certificate of title for the land; but absolutely free from all other encumbrances whatsoever
-- except the estate or interest of a proprietor claiming the same land under a prior registered certificate of title and
-- except as regards any portion of land that may by wrong description of parcels or boundaries be included in the
-- certificate ... not being a purchaser for valuable consideration or deriving from or through such a purchaser."
-- s 68(1A): "Despite subsection (1)" the land is deemed subject to the reservations, exceptions, conditions and powers in
-- the grant, "any rights subsisting under any adverse possession", "any public rights of way", "any easements acquired by
-- enjoyment or user or subsisting over or upon or affecting such land", "any unpaid rates", "any mining lease or licence
-- issued under the provisions of any statute", and a prior unregistered short lease (below) -- "notwithstanding the same
-- respectively may not be specially notified".
-- s 134: a transferee is not "affected by notice actual or constructive of any trust or unregistered interest ... and the
-- knowledge that any such trust or unregistered interest is in existence shall not of itself be imputed as fraud."
-- "Fraud" is not defined by the Act; whether my title is "a case of fraud" is a judgment for a court and is an input.
-- "Rates" is not defined in the deposit; whether a strata company's or community corporation's levies are "rates" is not
-- answered by this Act (c081, k076), and the encoding says so rather than guess.
DECLARE Interest IS ONE OF
    `an encumbrance notified on my certificate`
    `the estate of a proprietor under a prior registered certificate for the same land`
    `a reservation or condition in the Crown grant`
    `rights under adverse possession`
    `a public right of way`
    `an easement acquired by enjoyment or user`
    `unpaid rates`
    `a mining lease or licence issued under a statute`
    `an unregistered mortgage`
    `an unregistered interest I knew of when I took my transfer`
    `a trust not entered on my certificate`
    `unpaid levies of a strata company or community corporation`

DECLARE Bound IS ONE OF
    `bound: section 68 does not free me from it`
    `free: section 68 frees me from it`
    `unprotected: my title is a case of fraud, and section 68 frees me from nothing`
    `this Act does not say: whether such levies are unpaid rates is for the strata or community titles legislation`

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN Interest
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest binds me despite section 68` IF
    CONSIDER `the interest`
    WHEN `an unregistered mortgage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an unregistered interest I knew of when I took my transfer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a trust not entered on my certificate` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `unpaid levies of a strata company or community corporation` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Am I bound by this interest in my land, though my title is registered (s 68, s 134)?
GIVEN `the interest` IS AN Interest @desc The interest someone claims against your land
      `my title is a case of fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find your title a case of fraud (s 68 does not define fraud; knowing of an unregistered interest is not of itself fraud, s 134)
GIVETH A Bound
DECIDE `Am I bound by this interest` IS
    BRANCH IF `the interest binds me despite section 68` `the interest` THEN `bound: section 68 does not free me from it`
           IF `my title is a case of fraud` THEN `unprotected: my title is a case of fraud, and section 68 frees me from nothing`
           OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the interest`
                     WHEN `unpaid levies of a strata company or community corporation`
                         THEN `this Act does not say: whether such levies are unpaid rates is for the strata or community titles legislation`
                     OTHERWISE `free: section 68 frees me from it`

-- s 68(1A), the short lease: binding though unregistered only if "prior", for "a term not exceeding 5 years", and "to a
-- tenant in actual possession". A registered lease is notified on the certificate and binds under s 68(1).
`the longest unregistered lease that binds, in years` MEANS 5

@export Do I take my land subject to this lease (s 68(1), (1A))?
GIVEN `the lease is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lease is registered on the title
      `the lease came before my interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lease (or agreement for lease) existed before your interest
      `term of the lease in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The term of the lease, in years
      `the tenant is in actual possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the tenant is actually in possession of the land
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I take subject to the lease` IF
        `the lease is registered`
    OR  (    `the lease came before my interest`
         AND `term of the lease in years` AT MOST `the longest unregistered lease that binds, in years`
         AND `the tenant is in actual possession`)

-- s 68(1A) proviso: "no option of purchase or renewal in any such lease or agreement shall be valid as against a subsequent
-- registered interest unless such lease or agreement is registered or protected by caveat."
@export Is my tenant's option to buy or renew valid against me as a later registered owner (s 68(1A))?
GIVEN `the lease is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lease is registered
      `the lease is protected by caveat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a caveat protecting the lease is lodged
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the option valid against me` IF
    `the lease is registered` OR `the lease is protected by caveat`

§§ `199, 202, 201, 211, 214A -- who can take the land from me, and who pays when it is lost`

-- s 199: "Subject to sections 68 and 81T, no action of ejectment or other action for the recovery of any land shall lie or
-- be sustained against the person registered as proprietor" except: (a) a mortgagee against a mortgagor in default; (b) an
-- annuitant; (c) a lessor against a lessee in default; (d) "a person deprived of any land by fraud as against the person
-- registered as proprietor of such land through fraud or as against a person deriving otherwise than as a transferee bona
-- fide for value from or through a person so registered through fraud"; (e) misdescription, against a proprietor "not being
-- a transferee thereof bona fide for value"; (f) a proprietor under a certificate "prior in date of registration".
-- Otherwise the certificate "shall be held in every court to be an absolute bar and estoppel".
-- s 202: a "purchaser bona fide for valuable consideration" is not subject to ejectment because the proprietor through whom
-- he claims was registered through fraud or error.
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `my lender, after my default under the mortgage`
    `my landlord, after my default under the lease`
    `someone deprived by a fraud through which I was registered`
    `someone deprived by fraud, where I bought bona fide for value from the fraudster`
    `someone whose land was included in my title by misdescription, where I gave no value`
    `someone whose land was included in my title by misdescription, where I bought bona fide for value`
    `a proprietor under an earlier registered certificate for the same land`
    `someone with an unregistered interest`

@export Can this person bring an action to recover my land from me (ss 199, 202)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim @desc Who is claiming the land, and on what footing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can this person recover my land from me` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `someone deprived by fraud, where I bought bona fide for value from the fraudster` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `someone whose land was included in my title by misdescription, where I bought bona fide for value` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `someone with an unregistered interest` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 201(1): a person deprived of land "in consequence of fraud or through the bringing of such land under the operation of
-- this Act or by the registration of any other person as proprietor ... or in consequence of any error or misdescription"
-- may sue the person who acquired title through it. (2): outside fraud and that person's own error, a bona fide transfer for
-- value caps his liability at the consideration he received. (3): "In such lastmentioned case and also in case the person
-- against whom such action for damages is directed to be brought as aforesaid shall be dead or shall have been adjudged
-- bankrupt or cannot be found within the jurisdiction of the Supreme Court" damages and costs "may be recovered from the
-- State by action against the Registrar as nominal defendant". s 196 (cases where the State is not liable) is not encoded.
@export If I lose my land by fraud, error or someone else's registration, can I recover damages from the State (s 201)?
GIVEN `I was deprived by fraud, registration, error or misdescription` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lost the land (or an interest) through fraud, the bringing of land under the Act, another's registration, or an error or misdescription
      `the person liable is dead` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who acquired title through it is dead
      `the person liable is bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person has been adjudged bankrupt
      `the person liable cannot be found in the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person cannot be found within the jurisdiction of the Supreme Court
      `the person liable's liability is capped by a bona fide transfer for value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that person sold on bona fide for value, so that s 201(2) caps what they must pay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I recover damages from the State` IF
        `I was deprived by fraud, registration, error or misdescription`
    AND (    `the person liable is dead`
         OR  `the person liable is bankrupt`
         OR  `the person liable cannot be found in the jurisdiction`
         OR  `the person liable's liability is capped by a bona fide transfer for value`)

-- s 211(1): no action for damages for deprivation of land lies against the State "unless such action shall be commenced
-- within the period of 6 years from the date of such deprivation". (2): a person under "the disability of infancy or
-- unsoundness of mind" may sue "within 6 years from the date on which such disability shall have ceased so however that such
-- action be brought within 30 years next after the date of such deprivation". Counted in months: 72 and 360.
`the limitation period in months` MEANS 72
`the long stop in months` MEANS 360

@export Is it still time to sue for damages for losing my land (s 211)?
GIVEN `months since I was deprived` IS A NUMBER @desc Months from the date you lost the land to now
      `I was under a disability when deprived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a minor or of unsound mind when you lost the land
      `months since the disability ceased` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, months since the disability ended (0 if it has not ended or does not apply)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it still time to sue for my land` IF
        `months since I was deprived` AT MOST `the limitation period in months`
    OR  (    `I was under a disability when deprived`
         AND `months since the disability ceased` AT MOST `the limitation period in months`
         AND `months since I was deprived` AT MOST `the long stop in months`)

-- s 214A: "Any certificate of title, instrument, entry, erasure or alteration procured or made by fraud in any of the
-- circumstances set out in section 214 is void as against all persons who are party to that fraud, whether or not anyone is
-- convicted of that fraud." Conviction is not an input.
@export Is a title or instrument procured by fraud void against me (s 214A)?
GIVEN `it was procured by fraud in a section 214 circumstance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the certificate, instrument or entry was procured or made by fraud in a circumstance set out in s 214
      `I was party to the fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a party to that fraud
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it void against me` IF
    `it was procured by fraud in a section 214 circumstance` AND `I was party to the fraud`

§§ `60, 61 -- joint tenants, tenants in common, and "no survivorship"`

-- s 60: "Two or more persons who may be registered as joint proprietors of land shall be deemed to be entitled to the same
-- as joint tenants; and in all cases where 2 or more persons are entitled as tenants in common to undivided shares of or in
-- any land such persons may receive one certificate for the entirety or separate certificates for the undivided shares."
-- That is all s 60 says. It does not itself say that the survivor takes the whole; that is the general-law incident of a
-- joint tenancy (INFERENCE, not text).
DECLARE Holding IS ONE OF
    `as joint proprietors`
    `as tenants in common in undivided shares`
    `as sole proprietor`

@export Are my co-owner and I joint tenants (s 60)?
GIVEN `how we are registered` IS A Holding @desc How you and your co-owner(s) are registered on the title
      `number registered` IS A NUMBER @desc How many proprietors are registered
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are we joint tenants` IF
        `number registered` AT LEAST 2
    AND CONSIDER `how we are registered`
        WHEN `as joint proprietors` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@export May we take a separate certificate of title for each of our shares (s 60)?
GIVEN `how we are registered` IS A Holding @desc How you and your co-owner(s) are registered on the title
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we take separate certificates for our shares` IF
    CONSIDER `how we are registered`
    WHEN `as tenants in common in undivided shares` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 61(3): once the Registrar has signed the words "no survivorship", "it shall not be lawful for any persons other than the
-- proprietors registered to transfer or otherwise deal with the property without the order of the Supreme Court or a judge
-- thereof ... or the order of the Commissioner." The section does not say that the words end survivorship or make the owners
-- tenants in common; it says who may deal without an order.
@export May I deal with the property, where "no survivorship" is on the title (s 61)?
GIVEN `"no survivorship" has been signed by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the words "no survivorship" have been entered and signed by the Registrar
      `I am a registered proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of the registered proprietors
      `the Supreme Court or the Commissioner has ordered it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Supreme Court (or judge's) order, or the Commissioner's order, authorises your dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I deal with the property` IF
        (NOT `"no survivorship" has been signed by the Registrar`)
    OR  `I am a registered proprietor`
    OR  `the Supreme Court or the Commissioner has ordered it`

§§ `227, 187, 219, 220 -- onto the register after a death`

-- s 227: "Upon the death of any person registered with any other person as joint proprietor of any land ... the
-- Commissioner on the application of the person entitled and proof to his satisfaction of such events as aforesaid may
-- direct the Registrar to register such applicant as the proprietor thereof; and she or he shall upon being registered ...
-- become the transferee of such land ... and be deemed its proprietor." No probate is required by the section.
-- s 187(1): on an office copy of probate or letters of administration and "an application in writing of the executor,
-- administrator, or Public Trustee", the Registrar "shall" enter the appointment, and the legal personal representative
-- "shall become the transferee and be deemed to be the proprietor of the estate or interest of the deceased proprietor".
-- s 219(1): "A devisee or person claiming any estate of freehold in possession ... on a transmission may make application in
-- writing to the Commissioner to be registered as proprietor thereof and shall produce the will or an office copy or probate
-- of the will".
-- The Act does not say whether a deceased joint tenant's estate keeps any interest; that is general law (INFERENCE that it
-- does not, by survivorship). Land outside Western Australia is not "land under the operation of this Act".
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the surviving joint proprietor`
    `the executor or administrator`
    `a devisee under the will`
    `someone else`

DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `I may apply as survivor under section 227; no probate is needed`
    `I may apply as executor or administrator under section 187, on the probate or letters`
    `I may apply as devisee under section 219, producing the will or probate`
    `section 227 is the survivor's route; whether the deceased's estate keeps any interest is general law, not this Act`
    `this Act gives me no route onto the register for this land in that capacity`
    `the land is not under this Act, which says nothing about it`

@export How do I get onto the register for land of someone who has died (ss 187, 219, 227)?
GIVEN `the land is under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is Western Australian land registered under the Transfer of Land Act (land overseas or elsewhere in Australia is not)
      `how the deceased held it` IS A Holding @desc How the deceased was registered: as a joint proprietor, a tenant in common, or sole proprietor
      `my role` IS A Role @desc Who you are in relation to the land
GIVETH A Route
DECIDE `How do I get onto the register after the death` IS
    IF (NOT `the land is under this Act`)
    THEN `the land is not under this Act, which says nothing about it`
    ELSE CONSIDER `how the deceased held it`
         WHEN `as joint proprietors` THEN
             CONSIDER `my role`
             WHEN `the surviving joint proprietor` THEN `I may apply as survivor under section 227; no probate is needed`
             WHEN `someone else` THEN `this Act gives me no route onto the register for this land in that capacity`
             OTHERWISE `section 227 is the survivor's route; whether the deceased's estate keeps any interest is general law, not this Act`
         OTHERWISE
             CONSIDER `my role`
             WHEN `the executor or administrator` THEN `I may apply as executor or administrator under section 187, on the probate or letters`
             WHEN `a devisee under the will` THEN `I may apply as devisee under section 219, producing the will or probate`
             OTHERWISE `this Act gives me no route onto the register for this land in that capacity`

@export As the surviving joint proprietor, may the Commissioner direct my registration as sole proprietor (s 227)?
GIVEN `the deceased was registered with me as joint proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the deceased and you were registered as joint proprietors under this Act
      `I am the person entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are "the person entitled" (s 227 does not define it)
      `the death is proved to the Commissioner's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have proved the death to the Commissioner's satisfaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be registered as survivor` IF
        `the deceased was registered with me as joint proprietor`
    AND `I am the person entitled`
    AND `the death is proved to the Commissioner's satisfaction`

@export As executor or administrator, must the Registrar register me as proprietor of the deceased's interest (s 187(1))?
GIVEN `the Registrar has an office copy of the probate or letters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has received an office copy of the probate, letters of administration, or Public Trustee's order or election
      `I applied in writing to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied in writing to be registered as proprietor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Registrar register me as executor` IF
    `the Registrar has an office copy of the probate or letters` AND `I applied in writing to be registered`

-- s 187(3): "If in any case probate or administration is granted to more persons than one, all of them for the time being
-- shall join and concur in every dealing".
@export As one of several executors or administrators, may we deal with the land (s 187(3))?
GIVEN `number granted probate or administration` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people were granted probate or administration
      `number joining in the dealing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of them join in the dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we deal with the deceased's land` IF
    `number joining in the dealing` AT LEAST `number granted probate or administration`

-- s 220(1): the Commissioner "may either reject such application altogether or direct notice thereof to be published",
-- and "shall appoint a time not less than 14 days from the advertisement ... upon or after which the Registrar shall unless
-- a caveat shall be lodged forbidding the same register such applicant as the proprietor". (4): the Commissioner may direct
-- a caveat to protect others. Whether the Commissioner directs notice is the Commissioner's judgment, asked as a fact.
`the least notice period in days` MEANS 14

@export As a devisee who has applied under s 219, may the Registrar now register me (s 220)?
GIVEN `the Commissioner directed notice of my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner directed notice of your application to be published (rather than rejecting it)
      `days the Commissioner appointed` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days after the advertisement that the Commissioner appointed
      `days since the first advertisement` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the (first) advertisement
      `a caveat forbids my registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a caveat forbidding your registration has been lodged
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be registered as devisee` IF
        `the Commissioner directed notice of my application`
    AND `days since the first advertisement` AT LEAST `days the Commissioner appointed`
    AND `days since the first advertisement` AT LEAST `the least notice period in days`
    AND (NOT `a caveat forbids my registration`)

§§ `105, 105AA, 58, 106(1), 123 -- my mortgage: signature, effect, discharge`

-- s 105(3), (4): if the counterpart lodged "purports to be signed by the person who, on registration ... will become the
-- proprietor of the mortgage" but "does not purport to be signed by the proprietor of the land", no counterpart signed by the
-- proprietor is also lodged, and the instrument is registered, then "the mortgage or charge is not valid or binding against
-- the proprietor of the land unless, before the charging instrument was registered, the proprietor of the land signed a
-- counterpart". (5): "Subsection (4) overrides section 58." s 58: the land is liable to a mortgage only on registration.
DECLARE Mortgage HAS
    `registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the lender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I signed a counterpart before registration` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A Mortgage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 105(4) applies` IF
        `the mortgage`'s `registered`
    AND `the mortgage`'s `a lodged counterpart is signed by the lender`
    AND (NOT `the mortgage`'s `a lodged counterpart is signed by me`)

@export Does the mortgage over my land bind me (ss 58, 105(3)-(5))?
GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A Mortgage @desc The mortgage: whether registered, and who signed the counterparts lodged and before registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my mortgage bind me` IF
        `the mortgage`'s `registered`
    AND (    (NOT `section 105(4) applies` `the mortgage`)
         OR  `the mortgage`'s `I signed a counterpart before registration`)

-- s 105AA: "A mortgage must not be lodged electronically under the Electronic Conveyancing Act 2014 unless the mortgagee --
-- (a) has signed the mortgage instrument; and (b) holds a counterpart of the mortgage instrument signed by the proprietor of
-- the land."
@export May my lender lodge my mortgage electronically (s 105AA)?
GIVEN `the lender has signed the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender has signed the mortgage instrument
      `the lender holds a counterpart I signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender holds a counterpart of the mortgage signed by you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my lender lodge my mortgage electronically` IF
    `the lender has signed the mortgage` AND `the lender holds a counterpart I signed`

-- s 106(1): a mortgage "shall when registered ... have effect as a security but shall not operate as a transfer of the land
-- thereby mortgaged". I remain the registered proprietor.
DECLARE MortgageEffect IS ONE OF
    `a security over my land; I remain the proprietor and the land is not transferred`

@export What does registering my mortgage do to my title (s 106(1))?
GIVETH A MortgageEffect
DECIDE `What does my registered mortgage do` IS
    `a security over my land; I remain the proprietor and the land is not transferred`

-- s 123: on a memorandum "signed by the mortgagee ... and attested by a witness" discharging the land, the Registrar "shall
-- make an entry in the Register"; "upon such entry being made the land ... shall cease to be subject to or liable for such
-- moneys". Paying off the loan does not by itself clear the title; the entry does.
@export Is my land freed from the mortgage (s 123)?
GIVEN `the lender signed a witnessed discharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender signed a discharge, attested by a witness
      `the Registrar has entered the discharge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Registrar has entered the discharge in the Register
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my land freed from the mortgage` IF
    `the lender signed a witnessed discharge` AND `the Registrar has entered the discharge`

§§ `113, 88, 131 -- what my mortgage or my transfer binds me to without saying so`

-- s 113: implied in every mortgage, covenants by the mortgagor "that he or they will pay the principal money therein
-- mentioned on the day therein appointed", will pay interest "at the rate and on the days and in manner therein specified",
-- "will repair and keep in repair all buildings or other improvements", and that the mortgagee "may at all reasonable time
-- until such mortgage be redeemed enter into and upon such land ... to view and inspect". Insurance is not among them:
-- s 115 gives a short form that has effect only "whenever ... the mortgagor shall employ the form of words".
-- s 131: "Every covenant and power to be implied in any instrument by virtue of this Act may be negatived or modified by
-- express declaration in the instrument or endorsed thereon".
DECLARE Covenant IS ONE OF
    `to pay the principal on the day appointed`
    `to pay interest at the rate and on the days specified`
    `to keep the buildings and improvements in repair`
    `to let the lender enter at reasonable times to inspect`
    `to insure the buildings`

@export Does my mortgage bind me to this, though it does not say so (ss 113, 115, 131)?
GIVEN `the covenant` IS A Covenant @desc What you are asked whether you must do
      `the mortgage negatives or modifies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage expressly negatives or modifies that implied covenant (s 131)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my mortgage bind me to this` IF
        (NOT `the mortgage negatives or modifies it`)
    AND CONSIDER `the covenant`
        WHEN `to insure the buildings` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 88: in every transfer of land "subject to a mortgage or charge there shall be implied a covenant with the transferor by
-- the transferee" to pay the interest and to "indemnify and keep harmless the transferor ... from and against the principal
-- sum secured by the mortgage". s 131 lets it be negatived or modified.
@export As a buyer taking land subject to the seller's mortgage, must I indemnify the seller against it (ss 88, 131)?
GIVEN `I take the land subject to a mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your transfer is subject to a registered mortgage that stays on the title
      `the transfer negatives or modifies the covenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the transfer expressly negatives or modifies the implied covenant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I indemnify the seller` IF
    `I take the land subject to a mortgage` AND (NOT `the transfer negatives or modifies the covenant`)

§§ `106, 107, 108 -- my default, the notice, and the power of sale`

-- s 106(1): if default in payment or in a covenant "be continued for one month or for such other period of time as may
-- therein for that purpose be expressly fixed" the mortgagee "may serve on the mortgagor ... notice in writing to pay".
-- s 108: if the default continues "for one month after the service of such notice or for such other period as may in such
-- mortgage or charge be for that purpose fixed" the mortgagee "may sell the land mortgaged". Counted in months; a period the
-- mortgage fixes is entered in months, 0 meaning none fixed. (The Act puts no floor under the period the mortgage fixes.)
GIVEN `months fixed by the mortgage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months the default must continue` MEANS
    IF `months fixed by the mortgage` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `months fixed by the mortgage`
    ELSE 1

@export How many months must my default continue before my lender may serve a notice to pay (s 106(1))?
GIVEN `months fixed by the mortgage` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the mortgage expressly fixes for this, in months (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months before a notice to pay` IS `months the default must continue` `months fixed by the mortgage`

@export May my lender serve me a notice to pay (s 106(1))?
GIVEN `the mortgage is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage is registered
      `months my default has continued` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months your default has continued
      `months fixed by the mortgage for notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the mortgage fixes before notice, in months (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my lender serve a notice to pay` IF
        `the mortgage is registered`
    AND `months my default has continued` AT LEAST `months the default must continue` `months fixed by the mortgage for notice`

-- s 106(2): service "is not properly effected unless" the notice is (a) "delivered personally"; (b) "sent by registered
-- post" to (i) the address entered in the Register or (ii) the address known to the mortgagee as the current address; (c)
-- "left in a conspicuous place on the mortgaged or charged land"; or (d) sent "in compliance with a way of sending notices
-- electronically (for example, to an email address) that is prescribed by the regulations". s 106(3) keeps facsimile
-- service for those who elected it before the 2022 amendment: not encoded.
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `delivered to me personally`
    `registered post to my address in the Register`
    `registered post to my current address known to the lender`
    `left in a conspicuous place on the land`
    `an electronic way prescribed by the regulations`
    `ordinary post`
    `an email by a way not prescribed`

@export Has the notice to pay been properly served on me (s 106(2))?
GIVEN `how it was sent` IS A Service @desc How the lender sent or gave you the notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the notice properly served on me` IF
    CONSIDER `how it was sent`
    WHEN `ordinary post` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an email by a way not prescribed` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 107: where money secured "is made payable on demand a demand in writing pursuant to the mortgage shall be equivalent to
-- the notice in writing to pay ... and no other notice shall be required".
@export May my lender sell my land (ss 106-108)?
GIVEN `the money is payable on demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the mortgage makes the money payable on demand
      `a written demand was made under the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender made a written demand under the mortgage
      `a notice to pay was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lender served a notice to pay
      `how it was sent` IS A Service @desc How the notice was sent or given
      `months my default continued after the notice or demand` IS A NUMBER @desc Months your default has continued since the notice or demand
      `months fixed by the mortgage for sale` IS A NUMBER @desc The period the mortgage fixes after notice before sale, in months (0 if none)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my lender sell my land` IF
        (    (`the money is payable on demand` AND `a written demand was made under the mortgage`)
         OR  (`a notice to pay was served` AND `Was the notice properly served on me` `how it was sent`))
    AND `months my default continued after the notice or demand` AT LEAST `months the default must continue` `months fixed by the mortgage for sale`

§§ `109, 110 -- what happens to the sale money, and what the buyer at the lender's sale takes`

-- s 109(1): the purchase money "shall be applied as follows -- (a) firstly in payment of the expenses of and incidental to
-- such sale and consequent on such default; (b) secondly in payment of the moneys which may be due or owing on the mortgage;
-- (c) thirdly in payment of subsequent mortgages and of any money ... in respect of any subsequent charge in the order of
-- their respective priorities, and the surplus (if any) shall be paid to the mortgagor." (1A) (a subsequent annuity charge:
-- the money is deposited) is not encoded.
@export If my lender sells my land, how much of the sale money comes to me (s 109(1))?
GIVEN `the sale price` IS A NUMBER @desc The price the land sold for, in dollars
      `the expenses of the sale and default` IS A NUMBER @desc The expenses of and incidental to the sale and consequent on the default, in dollars
      `what is owing on the mortgage` IS A NUMBER @desc What is due or owing on the mortgage under which the land was sold, in dollars
      `what is owing on later mortgages and charges` IS A NUMBER @desc What is owing on mortgages and charges registered after it, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the sale money comes to me` IS
    IF `the sale price` MINUS `the expenses of the sale and default` MINUS `what is owing on the mortgage` MINUS `what is owing on later mortgages and charges` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the sale price` MINUS `the expenses of the sale and default` MINUS `what is owing on the mortgage` MINUS `what is owing on later mortgages and charges`
    ELSE 0

-- s 110: on registration of the mortgagee's transfer on sale the mortgagor's estate passes to the purchaser "freed and
-- discharged from all liability on account of such mortgage or charge and of any mortgage charge or encumbrance registered
-- subsequent thereto excepting a lease, carbon right, carbon covenant, plantation interest or grant of easement to which the
-- mortgagee ... shall have consented in writing". Encumbrances registered before the mortgage are not discharged.
@export As the buyer at a mortgagee's sale, do I take free of this encumbrance (s 110)?
GIVEN `it is the mortgage under which the land was sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the encumbrance is the selling lender's own mortgage
      `it was registered after that mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was registered after the selling lender's mortgage
      `it is a lease or easement the lender consented to in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a lease, easement, carbon right, carbon covenant or plantation interest that the selling lender consented to in writing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I take free of it` IF
        `it is the mortgage under which the land was sold`
    OR  (`it was registered after that mortgage` AND (NOT `it is a lease or easement the lender consented to in writing`))

§§ `121, 122 -- foreclosure of my right to redeem`

-- s 121(1): where default "shall be continued for 6 months after the time for payment mentioned in the mortgage, the
-- mortgagee ... may make application in writing to the Commissioner for an order for foreclosure". (1A): the application
-- must state that the land "has been offered for sale at public auction by a licensed auctioneer after notice to pay was
-- served in accordance with section 106", that the highest bid "was not sufficient to satisfy the moneys secured ... together
-- with the expenses" or "that there was no bid", and that notice of intention to apply has been served on the mortgagor and on
-- every person appearing by the Register to have a later interest.
`the default months before foreclosure` MEANS 6

@export May my lender apply to foreclose my right to redeem (s 121)?
GIVEN `months my default has continued after the time for payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the time for payment in the mortgage, with the default continuing
      `the land was offered at public auction after a properly served notice to pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a licensed auctioneer offered the land at public auction after a notice to pay was served under s 106
      `the auction raised too little or drew no bid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the highest bid was not enough to pay the mortgage money and expenses, or there was no bid
      `notice of intention to foreclose was served on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were served with notice of the lender's intention to apply for foreclosure
      `notice was served on every later registered interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether everyone with a later interest on the Register was served with the same notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my lender apply to foreclose` IF
        `months my default has continued after the time for payment` AT LEAST `the default months before foreclosure`
    AND `the land was offered at public auction after a properly served notice to pay`
    AND `the auction raised too little or drew no bid`
    AND `notice of intention to foreclose was served on me`
    AND `notice was served on every later registered interest`

-- s 122: the Commissioner "may direct" advertisement "once in each of the 3 successive weeks" offering the land for private
-- sale, and "shall appoint a time not less than one month from the date of the first of such advertisements upon or after
-- which the Registrar shall issue to such applicant an order for foreclosure, unless in the interval a sufficient amount has
-- been obtained by the sale of such land"; the order, when entered, vests the land in the mortgagee "free from all right and
-- equity of redemption on the part of the mortgagor".
@export Can a foreclosure order now issue and take my land (s 122)?
GIVEN `the Commissioner directed the advertisements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner directed the advertisements offering the land for private sale
      `months since the first advertisement` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the first advertisement
      `the time the Commissioner appointed has come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time the Commissioner appointed (at least one month after the first advertisement) has arrived
      `a sale in the interval raised enough` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sale in the meantime raised enough to pay the principal, interest and all expenses
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a foreclosure order issue against me` IF
        `the Commissioner directed the advertisements`
    AND `months since the first advertisement` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the time the Commissioner appointed has come`
    AND (NOT `a sale in the interval raised enough`)

§§ `138, 138A-138D, 139, 140, 142 -- caveats against my land`

-- s 137(1): a person claiming an estate or interest may lodge a caveat "forbidding the registration of any person as
-- transferee or proprietor of and of any instrument affecting such estate or interest". s 138(1): the Registrar notifies
-- the proprietor.
-- s 138A: the caveats to which ss 138B-138D apply are all except those lodged under ss 30, 176, 223A, "by or on behalf of a
-- beneficiary claiming under a will or settlement", "under a court order", "by the Registrar on the direction of the
-- Commissioner", under any other written law or Commonwealth Act, or by or with the consent of the Minister for Lands.
DECLARE CaveatKind IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary caveat claiming an interest`
    `a caveat by a beneficiary under a will or settlement`
    `a caveat by the Registrar on the Commissioner's direction`
    `a caveat lodged under a court order`
    `a caveat lodged under another written law or a Commonwealth Act`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A CaveatKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a section 138A caveat` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `an ordinary caveat claiming an interest` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 139(1): while a caveat remains in force the Registrar "shall not enter in the Register any change in the proprietorship
-- of or any transfer or other instrument" affecting the caveated interest, unless (2) applies, or the instrument is a
-- property (seizure and sale) order or sheriff's dealing (not encoded), or s 142 applies.
-- s 139(2): where "a caveat is lodged after the time of the presentation of the instrument, the caveat shall not have the
-- effect of preventing registration of the instrument".
-- s 142: a beneficiary's caveat does not bar a dealing if "the Commissioner is of opinion that such ... dealing is authorised
-- by the will or settlement and the caveator either consents to the registration or does not lodge a written protest
-- against such registration within 14 days after being served with notice". The Commissioner's opinion is asked as a fact.
`the protest period in days` MEANS 14

@export Does this caveat stop my dealing being registered (ss 139, 142)?
GIVEN `the caveat is in force and forbids the dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a caveat forbidding the dealing is in force on your title
      `it was lodged after my instrument was presented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveat was lodged after your instrument was presented for registration
      `the kind` IS A CaveatKind @desc What kind of caveat it is
      `the Commissioner thinks the will or settlement authorises my dealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a beneficiary's caveat: whether the Commissioner is of opinion the will or settlement authorises your dealing
      `the caveator consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveator consents to the registration
      `days since the caveator was served with notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the caveator was served with notice of the dealing
      `the caveator protested in writing in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveator lodged a written protest within 14 days of being served
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the caveat stop my dealing` IF
        `the caveat is in force and forbids the dealing`
    AND (NOT `it was lodged after my instrument was presented`)
    AND (NOT (    CONSIDER `the kind`
                  WHEN `a caveat by a beneficiary under a will or settlement` THEN TRUE
                  OTHERWISE FALSE
              AND `the Commissioner thinks the will or settlement authorises my dealing`
              AND (    `the caveator consents`
                   OR  (    `days since the caveator was served with notice` AT LEAST `the protest period in days`
                        AND (NOT `the caveator protested in writing in time`)))))

-- s 138(3): "Except in the case of a caveat lodged by or on behalf of a beneficiary claiming under any will or settlement or
-- by the Registrar pursuant to the direction of the Commissioner every caveat lodged against a proprietor shall be deemed to
-- have lapsed as to the land affected by the transfer or other dealing upon the expiration of 14 days after notice served on
-- the caveator that such proprietor has applied for the registration of a transfer or other dealing unless in the meantime
-- such application is withdrawn." (4): before then a judge may, on the caveator's undertaking or security, direct the
-- Registrar "to delay registering any dealing ... for a further period". Lapse is read as 14 full days having run.
`the lapsing period in days` MEANS 14

@export Has the caveat lapsed after I applied to register my dealing (s 138(3), (4))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A CaveatKind @desc What kind of caveat it is
      `I applied to register a transfer or dealing and have not withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to register a transfer or other dealing and the application stands
      `days since the caveator was served with notice of my application` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the caveator was served with notice of your application
      `a judge has ordered a further delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a judge, on the caveator's undertaking or security, directed the Registrar to delay registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the caveat lapsed on my dealing` IF
        (NOT (CONSIDER `the kind`
              WHEN `a caveat by a beneficiary under a will or settlement` THEN TRUE
              WHEN `a caveat by the Registrar on the Commissioner's direction` THEN TRUE
              OTHERWISE FALSE))
    AND `I applied to register a transfer or dealing and have not withdrawn`
    AND `days since the caveator was served with notice of my application` AT LEAST `the lapsing period in days`
    AND (NOT `a judge has ordered a further delay`)

-- s 138B(1): for a s 138A caveat "the proprietor of the land ... may apply ... for the Registrar to serve the caveator with a
-- notice to the effect that, unless the caveator takes the action referred to in subsection (2) within 21 days after the day
-- on which the notice is served, the caveat will lapse". (2): it lapses unless the caveator has obtained from the Supreme
-- Court an order extending it "and" lodged a copy with the Registrar. (s 138C: the Court extends only if "satisfied that the
-- caveator's claim has or may have substance" -- the Court's judgment, so whether an order was obtained is the input.)
`the extension notice period in days` MEANS 21

@export Has the caveat lapsed after the 21-day notice I had served (s 138B)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A CaveatKind @desc What kind of caveat it is
      `the Registrar served the caveator with my notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on your application, the Registrar served the caveator with the s 138B notice
      `days since the notice was served` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since the notice was served on the caveator
      `the caveator lodged a Supreme Court extension order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveator obtained a Supreme Court order extending the caveat and lodged a copy with the Registrar
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the caveat lapsed on my notice` IF
        `it is a section 138A caveat` `the kind`
    AND `the Registrar served the caveator with my notice`
    AND `days since the notice was served` AT LEAST `the extension notice period in days`
    AND (NOT `the caveator lodged a Supreme Court extension order`)

-- s 138D(1): if a s 138A caveat is withdrawn after a s 138B notice is served, has lapsed under s 138B(2), or no longer has
-- effect because of the Court's order or dismissal under s 138C, "the caveator cannot lodge ... any further section 138A
-- caveat in respect of the same land unless" the proprietor's consent is endorsed on it or the Supreme Court gives leave.
-- (2): withdrawal before any notice "does not prevent" a further caveat.
DECLARE CaveatEnd IS ONE OF
    `withdrawn before any 21-day notice was served`
    `withdrawn after the 21-day notice, before it could lapse`
    `lapsed under the 21-day notice`
    `ended by the Supreme Court's order or dismissal`

@export May the caveator lodge another caveat against my land (s 138D)?
GIVEN `how the caveat ended` IS A CaveatEnd @desc How the earlier caveat came to an end
      `my consent is endorsed on the new caveat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your consent is endorsed on the further caveat
      `the Supreme Court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court gave leave for the further caveat and the order was served on the Registrar
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the caveator lodge another caveat` IF
        `my consent is endorsed on the new caveat`
    OR  `the Supreme Court gave leave`
    OR  CONSIDER `how the caveat ended`
        WHEN `withdrawn before any 21-day notice was served` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 140: "Any person lodging any caveat ... without reasonable cause shall be liable to make to any person who may have
-- sustained damage thereby such compensation as a judge on a summons in chambers shall deem just and order." The amount is
-- the judge's; the encoding answers only whether the liability arises.
@export Can I be compensated for a caveat lodged against my land without reasonable cause (s 140)?
GIVEN `the caveat was lodged without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the caveat was lodged without reasonable cause
      `I suffered damage from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered damage because of it (for example, a lost or delayed sale)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be compensated for the caveat` IF
    `the caveat was lodged without reasonable cause` AND `I suffered damage from it`
